Enhancement: Warn about future-dated snapshots during check

Restic now warns when `check` finds a snapshot dated in the future relative
to the current system time. This can help explain why `forget --keep-within`
retains more snapshots than expected. The warning does not mark the repository
as damaged or change the command's exit status. JSON output reports it as a
`warning` message on stderr.

https://github.com/restic/restic/issues/3498
